# What NOT to upload to Railway.
#
# `railway up` tars the working directory. Unfiltered this repo is ~20 GB
# (models 15 G, data 3.2 G, .claude 1.2 G) and the upload would fail or take
# forever. The app image only needs source + lockfiles; persistent state lives
# on the mounted volume at runtime, not in the image.

# The native Windows desktop shell. Its Unisona.Shell.csproj makes Nixpacks
# detect a .NET app and run `dotnet restore` INSTEAD of installing Node — the
# 2026-08-21 build failed exactly this way (MSB1003: no project or solution
# file, because the .csproj is nested, not at the root it cd'd to).
apps/lantern-garage/desktop/

# Local model weights — never needed by the web server.
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Persistent state: this is the VOLUME's job. Mount it at /app/data.
# (Seed it separately; do not bake 3 GB of snapshots into the image.)
#
# Runtime state belongs on the volume, not in the image — EXCEPT data/contexts/,
# which is config rather than state: dream-chat.js reads personas.json from
# <repoRoot>/data/contexts directly (not via dataRoot()), so it has to be in the
# image.
#
# That works because the volume mounts at /app/state, NOT /app/data, with
# UNISONA_STATE_DIR=/app/state pointing the writable root at it (app-paths.js:
# "UNISONA_STATE_DIR, when set, wins outright"). Mounting on /app/data instead
# would shadow the image's config — which is how the first deploy ended up
# silently running with fallback personas.
#
# Note the `data/*` form, not `data/`: gitignore semantics do not allow
# re-including a path inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so `data/` + `!data/contexts/`
# silently ships nothing and the app boots with fallback personas. Excluding the
# directory's CONTENTS is what makes the negation effective.
data/*
!data/contexts/

# Agent/session scratch.
.claude/
.git/

# Installed at build time from the lockfiles.
node_modules/
apps/*/node_modules/

# Local-only research corpora and heavy artifacts.
arxiv-corpus/
experiments/results/
*.csf
*.zst

# Test/dev noise.
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.log
.env
.env.local
.env.*.bak*
